  "comment": "Every upstream input of the payload and the target kits, and the one table of platforms. Change versions here only; CI fetches, verifies and assembles. Each sha256 was checked against two independent downloads and against the digest the release publishes beside the asset. The server version is read from mcpp.toml. A platform is named <os>-<arch> as VS Code names extension targets; each row names the engine its payload entry carries, the target kit built for it (published as mcppls-kit-<kit.name>) and the target its test tools are built for. The VS Code extension, the CLion plugin, the release manifest and CI's matrices list the same platforms, which `mcppls-devtools check platforms` holds them to.",
